The cause of the consumed-but-never-run kicks (driver-27.2-diff.md §18.3):
with hardware data +0x2730 = 1 (as macOS writes) the firmware's queue
install writes nothing to the KSM and expects a host-side install. Leave it
0, as under 25G83, so the firmware installs the queues, and kick with the
tag-14 announcement (which advances the KSM kick count): items [lead],
configuration, announcement; no descriptor item, no event-254 hold.

